About Nebius:

Nebius is leading a new era in cloud infrastructure for the global AI economy. We are building a full-stack AI cloud platform that supports developers and enterprises from data and model training through to production deployment, without the cost and complexity of building large in-house AI/ML infrastructure.

Built by engineers, for engineers. From large-scale GPU orchestration to inference optimization, we own the hard problems across compute, storage, networking and applied AI.

Listed on Nasdaq (NBIS) and headquartered in Amsterdam, we have a global footprint with R&amp;D hubs across Europe, the UK, North America and Israel. Our team of 1,500+ includes hundreds of engineers with deep expertise across hardware, software and AI R&amp;D.

As Public Affairs Specialist - Finland, you will support and help deliver Nebius' public affairs strategy at national, regional and local levels. You will build trusted relationships with the President’s Office, Prime Minister’s Office, relevant ministries, Parliament and government agencies, while developing strong partnerships with municipalities, regional authorities, economic-development bodies, universities and communities. Working closely with all Nebius sites in Finland, including Mäntsälä and Lappeenranta, you will connect national policy engagement with local delivery, support Nebius ' strategic investment and infrastructure priorities, strengthen our license to operate and position the company as a responsible, long-term partner in Finland. The role has no fixed location requirement and involves regular travel to all Nebius sites in Finland and meetings with national, regional and local stakeholders. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

Key Responsibilities &nbsp;

• National government engagement . Support the development and execution of Nebius' public affairs strategy in Finland. Build relationships with the President’s Office, Prime Minister’s Office, relevant ministries, Parliament and government agencies. Prepare leadership engagement and secure support for Nebius' investment, AI infrastructure and skills initiatives.

• Regional and local engagement . Maintain close contact with all Nebius sites in Finland, including Mäntsälä and Lappeenranta, and drive engagement with mayors, municipalities, regional authorities, economic-development agencies, universities and communities. Develop initiatives that support local employment, Nebius Academy, education and community partnerships. Coordinate public-sector participation in site openings and investment announcements.

• Infrastructure and regulatory support . Anticipate and address public affairs issues related to data- centre development, grid access, electricity taxation, permitting, planning and environmental requirements. Engage with relevant authorities, Fingrid , local grid operators and energy partners. Support advocacy on predictable investment conditions, waste-heat reuse and community impact, and translate policy developments into clear business recommendations.

• Strategic advocacy and coalition building . Develop policy positions on AI infrastructure, cloud, industrial competitiveness, strategic autonomy, energy and sustainability. Position Nebius ’ investments in terms of their contribution to Finland’s AI capabilities, research, skills and economic development. Build coalitions with industry associations, technology and energy partners, think tanks and universities.

• Executive advice and internal alignment . Provide leadership with concise advice on political developments, stakeholder priorities, risks and opportunities. Prepare briefings, talking points and policy materials, and coordinate closely with Infrastructure, Legal, Compliance, Communications, Finance, HR, Sustainability and commercial teams. &nbsp;

Key Qualifications &amp; Experience

Must-have requirements: &nbsp;

• At least five years of relevant experience : in public affairs, government relations, public policy, political advisory or external relations.

BeOne continues to grow at a rapid pace with challenging and exciting opportunities for experienced professionals. When considering candidates, we look for scientific and business professionals who are highly motivated, collaborative, and most importantly, share our passionate interest in fighting cancer.
General Description:

The Senior Contract Associate is responsible for drafting, negotiating, and finalizing complex Clinical Site Contracts related to clinical trials throughout the lifecycle of the study, and performs timely and accurate data entry into all Clinical Business Operations operating systems, including but not limited to the company Contract Management System (CMS). The Contract Associate is also responsible for meeting deliverables with high quality and within the project timelines. The contracting activity supported by the CBO team is fast-paced, with short deadlines and quick turnaround times therefore Contract Associate must be capable of managing priorities effectively, proactively communicating issues and working in a fast-paced environment.

Essential Functions of the job:

• Prepare, negotiate, and finalize clinical trial agreements, ancillary agreements and amendments of company sponsored studies through direct communication with sites.

• Responsible for execution of contracts against planned timelines and targets.

• Manage budget grid in the contract. Ensure the cost calculation are consistent with protocol and agreed with site.

• Demonstrates an understanding of records management requirements for contract documents

• Complete quality check (QC) of final approved contract and budget documents, and initiates signature process of assigned contracts to the responsible signing parties.

• Ensure final contracts are delivered to agreed timelines, within Fair Market Value & in compliance with relevant legal and regulatory requirements

• Serve as the primary point of contact between CBO and Global Clinical Operations (GCO), Legal, Investigator Sites and external service providers in accordance with the study related activities to meet business needs;

• Collect and maintain country and site intelligence information for each country and/or site, and prepares country/site specific contract process flows as needed;

• Forecast, set, track and communicate fully executed contract planned dates, and make all efforts to achieve the set planned date, ensuring the CM and study teams are proactively informed of changes and/or risks to the projected dates;

• Liaise with CM and BeOne legal to review and update contract template(s) as needed, including Master Clinical Trial Agreements/Clinical Trial Agreements/Project Agreements or any other Site agreement template(s);

• Liaise with CM and BeOne legal to contribute updates to the BeOne Legal Playbook guidance document as needed;

• Liaise with Investigator Payment Management (IPM) team to ensure site contracts, including investigator site budgets, are approved and executed in accordance with CBO guidelines and BeOne policies;

• Ensure all investigator contracts are reviewed and approved by legal and/or delegate prior to execution, and in accordance with CBO and BeOne legal guidelines;

• Communicate legal and budgetary issues to internal and external parties per department guidelines, as needed;

• Perform legal translation of contract language for Sites, as needed;

• Maintain active and regular communication with site personnel and internal BeOne partners, with regular progress tracking and updates provided throughout the contract lifecycle;

